            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a claim, then the Telugu for a reform."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: సమాజం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సమాజం — samājaṁ — \"society; a community\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సమాజంలో ప్రతి ఒక్కరికీ ఒక బాధ్యత ఉంది. samājaṁlō prati okkarikī oka bādhyata undi. Everyone has a responsibility in society."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also a smaller community: మన సమాజం (samājaṁ), our community."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సమాజం (samājaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit samāja, \"a festive gathering\" (CDIAL 13207), which Monier-Williams also glosses \"an assembly, a society\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
